# Windows scripts keep Windows line endings in every download (launch.ps1 is also kept pure ASCII).
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
# Everything else is normalised; images and fonts are binary.
* text=auto
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
# Files the checks write and then compare as they are on disk keep LF in every checkout, so a fresh Windows clone
# passes the same checks as any other: the legal pages and documents (node verify-legal.cjs --write), the loading
# card's colour table in public/index.html (node verify-theme.cjs --write) and the spell reports the spell checks
# rewrite. The checks also read these files without regard to line endings, for checkouts made before this.
public/*.html text eol=lf
PRIVACY.md text eol=lf
TERMS.md text eol=lf
PERMISSIONS.md text eol=lf
SPELL-*.json text eol=lf
